---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Niusha Sedgh | Electrical Engineering & Robotics"
  description="Academic portfolio of Niusha Sedgh, an electrical engineering student working on control, robotics, autonomous systems, and intelligent technologies."
>
  <div class="space-y-16">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[1.5fr_0.8fr] md:items-center">

      <div class="space-y-6">

        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-600">
            Electrical Engineering · Control · Robotics
          </p>

          <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 md:text-5xl">
            Niusha Sedgh
          </h1>
        </div>

        <p class="max-w-2xl text-xl leading-8 text-slate-600">
          Electrical engineering student interested in 
          
             control systems, robotics, and autonomous systems
          
          with a focus on combining classical control with
          AI-driven methods for intelligent autonomous platforms.
        </p>

        <p class="max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-slate-500">
          My work explores areas such as intelligent control, reinforcement
          learning, autonomous vehicles, multi-agent systems, sensor fusion,
          and navigation. I use this website to document my research,
          engineering projects, publications, and ongoing work.
        </p>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 pt-2">

          <a
            href="/projects"
            class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-white
                   hover:bg-slate-700 transition-colors"
          >
            View Projects
          </a>

          <a
            href="/publications"
            class="rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-5 py-3 text-sm
                   font-medium text-slate-700 hover:border-indigo-300
                   hover:text-indigo-700 transition-colors"
          >
            Publications
          </a>

          <a
            href="/contact"
            class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 px-5 py-3 text-sm
                   font-medium text-slate-600 hover:border-slate-300
                   hover:text-slate-900 transition-colors"
          >
            Contact
          </a>

        </div>
      </div>

       <!-- Current Status -->
      <aside class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">

        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500">
          Current Status
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 space-y-4">

          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-600">
              Bachelor Thesis
            </p>

            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
              Hybrid intelligent control architecture for vehicle platooning
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-violet-600">
              Current Stage
            </p>

            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">
              Literature review, system design, and research development
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

      </aside>

    </section>
      
    <!-- Current Focus -->
    <section class="border-t border-slate-200 pt-12">

      <div class="max-w-4xl">

        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-600">
          Current Focus
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
          Developing a Hybrid Control Architecture for Vehicle Platooning
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-8 text-slate-600">
          My current focus is my bachelor's thesis, which explores a
          multi-layer control architecture for autonomous vehicle platooning.
          The main idea is to combine learning-based decision making with
          model-based control and a digital-twin layer to improve both
          performance and safety.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">

        <!-- RL -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-600">
            01 · Learning Layer
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">
            Reinforcement Learning
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Exploring reinforcement learning as a high-level decision-making
            layer for long-term planning and optimization in vehicle platooning.
          </p>

        </div>


        <!-- MPC -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-violet-600">
            02 · Safety Layer
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">
            Model-Based Control
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Studying MPC and related control methods as a lower-level mechanism
            for maintaining stability, constraint satisfaction, and safe vehicle
            operation.
          </p>

        </div>


        <!-- Digital Twin -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-600">
            03 · Validation Layer
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">
            Digital Twin
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Investigating how a digital-twin representation can be used to
            evaluate proposed actions and estimate potentially unsafe
            situations before commands are applied to the physical system.
          </p>

        </div>


        <!-- Safety -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">

          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600">
            04 · Safety Mechanism
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">
            Safe Decision Making
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
            Exploring mechanisms that allow the architecture to fall back to
            model-based control when a learned action is predicted to violate
            safety constraints or increase collision risk.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- Bottom CTA -->
    <section class="text-center py-4">

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">
        Interested in research or collaboration?
      </h2>

      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600">
        Feel free to get in touch for academic discussions and research opportunities.
      </p>

      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="inline-flex mt-5 rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 px-5 py-3 text-sm
               font-medium text-white hover:bg-indigo-700 transition-colors"
      >
        Get in Touch
      </a>

    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>